{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 3"},"body":"Link the end-replacement result, not the conditional Bondi-Penrose inequality endpoint.\n\nInspected: Read both configured theorem declarations, ambient connected smooth three-manifold assumptions, CKSData, PhysicalDEC, minimumEnclosingArea and SchwarzschildExample; exact prop:replacement.","content_sha256":"sha256:687f911436f68101a53954542eae0290dd478435e4eece325873e09b9906f5eb","fingerprint":"sha256:d47dfa1722fc430d94850cd592866e0e2587755b6204b6e61aa18ccde6dc8e62","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Link the end-replacement result, not the conditional Bondi-Penrose inequality endpoint.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:079b6e8e26bec3dc1c67cd4aacc0bbc2af008adef3615599e3b9de2bebde686d","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.CKSSourceExterior.area_controlled_end_replacement"],"explanation":"The configured area-controlled replacement theorem preserves the original data inside a large radius, preserves DEC and completeness, and bounds the replacement metric below by (1-epsilon_R)g with epsilon_R tending to zero. Its asymptotically flat end has zero momentum and energy m_B+eta_R with 0≤eta_R≤2R^-1/2, and it supplies the minimum-enclosing-area comparison of the replacement proposition.","fingerprint":"sha256:f30c07ca18e6d92538340ca4aaace062eeb8718202bfa9f1da0a2222f2f8d7f2","limitations":"The separately configured Schwarzschild equality examples are not represented by this link. Detailed differential-geometric definitions beyond the inspected source assumptions were not independently certified.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026#prop:replacement","statement_sha256":"sha256:9d7ab105b477f2cfbffefec8a12cd8c5ba5aac52b577548416150bb0aa65b070"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/CKSBondiPenrose.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L128"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:CKSBondiPenrose","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":false,"detail":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.CKSSourceExterior.area_controlled_end_replacement","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/CKSBondiPenrose.lean","line":3312,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"079b6e8e26bec3dc1c67cd4aacc0bbc2af008adef3615599e3b9de2bebde686d","statement_sha256":"sha256:d04db8b345bba2204ac7a42a9642c3aef6b3c53906a88771056e1003e28cdc6a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/CKSBondiPenrose.lean#L3312"},"text":"theorem area_controlled_end_replacement\n    (g : OAI.CKSMetricGluing.SmoothMetric OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 (M := N)) (K : OAI.CKSMetricGluing.InnerField OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 (M := N))\n    (hK : ContMDiff OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 (OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3.prod 𝓘(ℝ,OAI.CKSLorentz.SpatialBilinear)) ∞ (OAI.CKSMetricGluing.innerSection OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 K))\n    (hKsym : ∀ x v w, K x v w = K x w v)\n    (hOrient : OAI.CKSSourceExterior.Orientable (N := N))\n    (hScompact : IsCompact (OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3.boundary N)) (hSnonempty : (OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3.boundary N).Nonempty)\n    (hcomplete : OAI.CKSReplacementCompleteness.IsComplete OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 g.toContinuousRiemannianMetric)\n    (hDEC : OAI.CKSSpatialManifold.PhysicalDEC OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 g.inner K)\n    (d : OAI.CKSSourceExterior.CKSData g K)\n    (ht : ‖(OAI.CKSLorentz.bondiCharge d.massAspect).2‖ < (OAI.CKSLorentz.bondiCharge d.massAspect).1) :\n    ∃ (d' : OAI.CKSSourceExterior.CKSData g K) (R₀ : ℝ) (ε : ℝ → ℝ),\n      OAI.CKSLorentz.bondiCharge d'.massAspect =\n        (Real.sqrt ((OAI.CKSLorentz.bondiCharge d.massAspect).1^2 - ‖(OAI.CKSLorentz.bondiCharge d.massAspect).2‖^2),0) ∧\n      d'.chart.radius < R₀ ∧ 12 ≤ R₀ ∧ Tendsto ε atTop (𝓝 0) ∧\n      OAI.CKSFullCutArea.minEnclosingArea g < ⊤ ∧\n      ∀ R ≥ R₀, (0 ≤ ε R ∧ ε R < 1) ∧\n        ∃ (gR : OAI.CKSMetricGluing.SmoothMetric OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 (M := N)) (kR : OAI.CKSMetricGluing.InnerField OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 (M := N))\n          (G k : OAI.CKSLorentz.SpatialTensor) (η : ℝ),\n          ContMDiff OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 (OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3.prod 𝓘(ℝ,OAI.CKSLorentz.SpatialBilinear)) ∞ (OAI.CKSMetricGluing.innerSection OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 kR) ∧\n          (∀ x v w, kR x v w = kR x w v) ∧\n          (∀ x, x ∉ d'.chart.domain ∨ ‖d'.chart.coordinate x‖ ≤ R →\n            gR.inner x = g.inner x ∧ kR x = K x) ∧\n          OAI.CKSSpatialManifold.PhysicalDEC OAI.CKSGeometricCuts.I3 gR.inner kR ∧\n          (∀ x v, (1-ε R) * g.inner x v v ≤ g"},{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/1"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.CKSMain.schwarzschild_equality_examples","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/CKSBondiPenrose.lean","line":3591,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"079b6e8e26bec3dc1c67cd4aacc0bbc2af008adef3615599e3b9de2bebde686d","statement_sha256":"sha256:ef12be667939f85788bfc21e885fb9b750be29282a02278d28f173d4f58588f5","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/CKSBondiPenrose.lean#L3591"},"text":"theorem schwarzschild_equality_examples (m : ℝ) (hm : 0 < m) :\n    SchwarzschildExample.{v} m hm"}],"state":"partial","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"l:CKSBondiPenrose","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[{"kind":"text","path":"lean/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0/text","returned_chars":2000,"total_chars":3333}],"pairings":{"f:260":{"alternatives":["pair:23ac81122dd299d524347b10"],"contributed_readings":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 3"},"content_sha256":"sha256:687f911436f68101a53954542eae0290dd478435e4eece325873e09b9906f5eb","decision":"linked","detail":{"path":"lean-previews/53a9604d749b739277fbaec9.json","pointer":"/contributions/0"},"provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"review_state":"unreviewed","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.CKSSourceExterior.area_controlled_end_replacement"],"limitations":"The separately configured Schwarzschild equality examples are not represented by this link. Detailed differential-geometric definitions beyond the inspected source assumptio